  "question": {
    "text": "Two spherical soap bubbles of radii <math><mi>a</mi></math> and <math><mi>b</mi></math> in vacuum coalesce under isothermal conditions. The resulting bubble has a radius given by"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><msqrt><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, the bubbles coalesce in vacuum and there is no change in temperature, hence its surface energy does not change. This means that the surface area remains unchanged. Hence,<br/><br/><math><mn>4</mn><mi> </mi><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow><mi> </mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi> </mi><mi>π</mi><mi> </mi><msup><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><mi> </mi><msup><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> or <math><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt></math>"
  }
